DESCRIPTION:Get ready for a special girls’ night out presented by Group C
 hat Girlies.\n\nSkylar Schock and Carol Tyner host a one-of-a-kind evening 
 made just for the girlies.\n\nEnjoy\nstand up comedy\, interactive segments
 \, and unpacking what's in the\ngroup chat. We plan to “spill the tea”\
 , share recommendations\, discuss\npop culture and more. Think your group c
 hat — but in person\, on stage\,\nwith plenty of audible gasps and laughs
 .\n\nGirlie fight club is here.\n\nSkylar\nSchock and Carol Tyner are known
  for their sharp\, relatable takes on\ndating\, friendship\, and all things
  girlhood. This show blends comedy and\nconversations in a unique format.\n
 \nSkylar is a bi-coastal stand-up\ncomic\, actor\, writer\, and producer. S
 he has performed across the\ncountry at venues including The Comedy Store (
 La Jolla)\, Jimmy Kimmel’s\nComedy Club (Las Vegas)\, and the Laugh After
  Dark stage. She's opened\nfor headliners including Cristina Mariani\, Mich
 ael Yo\, John Caparulo\,\nand Ivy Wolk. Skylar was a Best of Fest selection
  at the Comedy Chateau\nComedy Festival (LA)\, an official performer at the
  Queen City Comedy\nExperience (CLT) and advanced in the WSOC (ATL and Ohio
 ). She is the\ncreator of Group Chat Girlies\, a unique format live show\, 
 and Laugh\nUntil You Cry\, a stand-up show spotlighting mental health. Film
  credits\ninclude For the Love of Lily and the Austin Film Fest Award-winni
 ng\nshort Betsy F*ing Ross.\n\nCarol Tyner is a stand-up comedian\,\nimprov
 iser\, and producer. Carol has performed at comedy clubs including\nThe Idi
 ot Box Comedy Club\, The Comedy Club at Duckworth’s\, The Comedy\nZone (C
 harlotte & Greenville). She has opened for headliners\nincluding Tim Meadow
 s\, Erica Rhodes\, Cliff Cash\, Cam Bertrand\, and\nConner King. Carol has 
 been a featured performer in festivals including:\nThe North Carolina Comed
 y Festival\, The Queen City Comedy\nExperience\,\, The NewSouth Comedy Fest
 ival\, and The Asheville Comedy\nFestival. She is a founding cast member of
  the award-winning Shameless\nImprov Society. Carol also co-produces…\nMo
